@format 1
@id edit.change-crop
@title Change Crop, rotation, or flip
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Apply Crop edges, Reset, ratio presets, rotation or flip, or viewer-rectangle changes to the Edit preview and request persistence of the active source plan.
@section I. UI
@tabs Edit
@flow TB
@related edit.save-plan, edit.restore-plan

@alias inspector = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PInspector
@alias tab = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PEditTab

[input] Crop state changes <input>
- Enable or disable the Crop state and refresh its editor surface @ inspector.PInspectorApplyUpdate(...)
- Publish a changed Crop rectangle from inset, ratio, or viewer-drawing input @ inspector.PInspectorCropRaise(...)
- Reset all four Crop edges without changing ratio, rotation, flip, Apply, or persistence settings @ inspector.PInspectorEdgesReset(...)
- Fit a selected ratio preset to the largest centered even-pixel rectangle inside the current Crop or full frame @ inspector.PInspectorRatioPresetHandle(...)
- Publish a changed rotation or flip state @ inspector.PInspectorRotateRaise(...)
- Convert a ratio constraint into a viewer Crop ratio @ inspector.PInspectorRatioUpdate(...)
- Recompute the read-only resulting resolution from the source and effective even Crop edges @ inspector.PInspectorResolutionUpdate(...)
> preview

[preview] Synchronize Crop preview <process>
- Apply Crop events to the viewer through the Edit-tab event subscriptions @ tab.PEditTab(...)
- Apply rotation to the viewer and synchronize the inspector with the rotated source dimensions @ tab.PEditRotateHandle(...)
- Update inspector Crop state when the viewer reports an adjusted rectangle @ tab.PEditCropShow(...)
- Save Crop or rotation changes for the active source through the Edit-tab event subscriptions @ tab.PEditTab(...)
> persist

[persist] Continue to plan persistence <output>
> map:edit.save-plan
